From: Qianzf <qianzf@users.noreply.github.com>
Subject: [PATCH] net: ppe: clear the NAPI dummy netdev pointer after freeing it

ppe_ds_free() frees ds->napi_dev but leaves the pointer in place before
kfree()ing the DS object, so a repeated qcom_ppe_ds_unregister() on the
same handle walks freed memory and calls free_netdev() again, which ends
in dev_addr_check() dereferencing NULL after dev_addr_flush().

Clear the field while the DS object is still valid. This does not make
qcom_ppe_ds_unregister() idempotent (it frees the handle itself), it only
keeps the failure mode of a duplicated teardown from being a NULL pointer
oops on a released net_device.
---
--- a/drivers/net/ethernet/qualcomm/ppe/ppe_ds.c
+++ b/drivers/net/ethernet/qualcomm/ppe/ppe_ds.c
@@ -592,6 +592,7 @@ static void ppe_ds_free(struct qcom_ppe_ds *ds)
 	if (ds->napi_dev) {
 		netif_napi_del(&ds->napi);
 		free_netdev(ds->napi_dev);
+		ds->napi_dev = NULL;
 	}
 	if (ds->fill)
 		dma_free_coherent(dev, rx * sizeof(*ds->fill), ds->fill, ds->fill_dma);
